      "id": "rdls_exp-ken_rcmrd_kilifisurveillancedata",
      "title": "Kilifi_Surveillance_Data",
      "description": "This dataset provides records of pest/disease occurrences in maize/bean/potato across Kilifi County in Kenya collected under the Risk Management System for Plant Pests and Diseases project. The data includes details on the geographich location, date of occurrence, type of crop affected, type of pest/disease, stage of growth/severity of disease. It integrates surveillance reports, Earth observation data, and field survey information to support early warning, response planning, and risk mitigation strategies. The dataset is designed to aid policymakers, researchers, and farmers in monitoring trends and making informed decisions to manage the pest/disease risk and therefore enhance food security. It is available in geospatial formats, ensuring compatibility with mapping and decision-support tools. Data accuracy was ensured through validation against historical records and expert assessments. Access is subject to licensing conditions as outlined by the Plant Protection and Food Safety Directorate (PPFSD) and the Regional Centre for Mapping of Resources for Development (RCMRD). [Source: This metadata record was automatically extracted from the GeoNode portal rcmrd]",
